    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for grafana.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 10.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "Grafana is an open source, feature rich metrics dashboard and graph editor for Graphite, InfluxDB & OpenTSDB. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* grafana: Azure Monitor data source could leak its Azure access token (CVE-2026-88967)\n\n* github.com/klauspost/compress/zstd: klauspost/compress: Denial of Service via crafted zstd compressed input (CVE-2026-116591)\n\n* grafana: Grafana: Information disclosure via legacy schema switch in contact points (CVE-2026-100105)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
        "category": "legal_disclaimer",
        "text": "This content is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). If you distribute this content, or a modified version of it, you must provide attribution to the original copyright holder(s) and provide a link to the original.",
